Restore the original packed memory-card menu WORD fields and sprite buffers.
FUN_0044a314 writes WORD underline lengths at 0x4671ce/0x4671da
(MOV WORD at 0x44a37a/0x44a381 and 0x44a3e8/0x44a3ef). DWORD
assignments erased the adjacent red/green bytes: the Save underline used
index 201 instead of original index 2 across 488 pixels. LoadSave, block
selection, confirmation and name entry also use MOV WORD for their packed
x/y sprite/text coordinates (0x467150..0x4673de); DWORD x erased y.
FUN_0044a050 copies six DWORDs into each 24-byte descriptor at ebp-0x24
and ebp-0x3c (REP MOVSD at 0x44a077/0x44a093), then sets y at +2
(MOV WORD at 0x44a095/0x44a099). Ghidra split these buffers into
independent shorts; reconstruct contiguous arrays for the tick/cross.

